[agent] ## Summary
[agent] I logged the deployed model's predictions into the Hopsworks feature store and used the platform's statistics/SQL engine to detect the distribution shift.
[agent] **What I did (all platform-side via the `hops` CLI):**
[agent] 1. Created feature group `prediction_log` (v1) with `ts` (string, primary key) and `prediction` (double).
[agent] 2. Ingested all 13,307 logged predictions with `hops fg insert --file data/prediction_log.csv`.
[agent] 3. Computed per-day prediction statistics on the platform with `hops trino sql` (Trino over the offline Delta table), grouping by day to get daily `count`, `mean`, and `stddev`.
[agent] **Finding:** The daily mean prediction is stable at ~7.9 (sd ~0.75) from 2026-01-01 through **2026-02-15**, then jumps to ~11.0 (sd ~0.75) on **2026-02-16** and remains there through 2026-03-31. The spread is unchanged — it's a clean level shift in the mean of ~+3.1. The changepoint is sharp (single-day jump between consecutive days), so the onset is unambiguous.
[agent] **Deliverable written to `submission/answers.json`:**
[agent] ```json
[agent] {"onset": "2026-02-16"}
[agent] ```
